.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-audit - Audit workspace versions, dependencies, agents and delivery


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit audit [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Report drift between the workspace and manovaspace/ci/ci/versions.env, resolved dependency versions, kit exports shadowed by local code, agent configuration, repositories without tests, upstream toolchain lag and merge-gate bypasses. The audit is read-only: it never edits a repository and reads the network only with --remote on the checks that support it. Exit codes: 0 no ERROR findings, 1 at least one ERROR, 2 something could not be verified.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for audit

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print the report as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--remote\fP[=false]
	Also run the network checks (registry, OSV, releases, merges, Actions billing)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-agents(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-deps(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-merges(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-tests(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-upstream(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-usage(1)\fP, \fBorbit-audit-versions(1)\fP
